# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Moved from an inline build.sh
# --check block by the .step series (batch 3, 2266: the slowest blocks first,
# measured one at a time on lenovinha). As a .step it is no build.sh edit, so it
# never makes intake HEAVY; it runs SERIAL on its lane, beside the other lanes.
#
# 956-llei: the kill-time adjudicator must diff THIS cgroup's cpu.pressure
# stall counter across the step's own window and say CONTENDED / NOT
# contended / UNCLASSIFIED — never the retired host-wide load1-vs-ncpus
# rule, which judged forge steps by the host's runqueue. Three arms, run
# through the real runner in a temp root with injected counters.
STEP_DESC="Checking the kill-time adjudicator diffs cpu.pressure (956-llei)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-litmus-kill-adjudicator.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the litmus kill-time adjudicator does not classify by cpu.pressure diff (956-llei) — see the verdict line above"
STEP_OK="Litmus kill-time adjudicator check passed"
STEP_SERIAL="runs the real litmus runner"
STEP_LANES="litmus"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-11-26 darwin ok:litmus-kill-adjudicator:7 arms (work/2387-lrg2 @ 4e3a2a540)"
STEP_READS="scripts/lua/test-litmus-kill-adjudicator.lua"
